{
  "id": "ar_practical",
  "title": "Arabic — practical English romanization (newspaper style)",
  "language": "ar",
  "script": "Arab",
  "kind": "practical",
  "status": "informal",
  "ascii": true,
  "authority": "Common English-language press and government practice (ODNI ICS 630-01 style, diacritics stripped); not a formal standard",
  "description": "Readable ASCII spellings as used in English-language media: known names come from the lexicon (Muhammad, Abdullah), other names are vocalised from common name patterns and written without diacritics: h for ح, s for ص, kh, sh, th, dh, gh, q; ʿayn and hamza dropped; long vowels unmarked; ة = a; article al- without assimilation; Abd al-X becomes Abdul X.",
  "sources": [
    "https://github.com/interscript/maps/blob/main/maps/odni-ara-Arab-Latn-2015.isc",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Arabic",
    "https://itftennis.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1272938619/Passport%20Standards.pdf?api=v2"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Lexicon spellings (latin['ar']) win; the rules below only handle vocalised input and names the lexicon does not know (unknown bare names are vocalised by templates: فاعل Khalid, فعيل Karim, مفعول Mahmud, أفعل Ahmad, فَعْلَل Jafar …).",
    "Shadda doubles the letter, except digraphs and ʿayn (Bashar, not Bashshar; Qadhafi, not Qadhdhafi), as in ODNI ICS 630-01.",
    "ʿayn after a and before a consonant is written as a second a (Saad, Jaafar); elsewhere it is dropped (Ali, Said).",
    "ة is a (Fatima), but t after ā (Hayat, Najat); ى is a (Mustafa); final -iyy is i (Ali).",
    "Article: al- + name without sun-letter assimilation (al-Rashid); عبد ال… → Abdul … (Abdul Rahman, Abdul Aziz); عبد الله → Abdullah; بن → bin, ابن → ibn."
  ],
  "alphabet": "ءآأؤإئابةتثجحخدذرزسشصضطظعغفقكلمنهوىيٱپچژگڤ",
  "hook": "arabic",
  "options": {
    "practical": ["ar"],
    "vocalize": true,
    "article": "al-"
  },
  "geminate": "\u0651",
  "titlecase": true,
  "lowercase_words": ["al-", "bin", "ibn", "bint"],
  "fallback": "ascii",
  "aliases": {"ی": "ي", "ک": "ك", "ڪ": "ك", "ہ": "ه", "ھ": "ه", "ۀ": "ه", "ە": "ه", "ۃ": "ة", "ې": "ي", "ے": "ي"},
  "classes": {
